#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110292 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e8c4c24-2d04-5fd1-a9f4-6f1abb25c255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Smaller Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "d4240cff-2c48-520b-a11a-f6838c163a17" :question/math-academy-id "e-10594" :question/problem "The measure of the angle $\\angle BAD$ is ${90}^{\\circ}.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n![](images/f4/f41802149d3e2a8524a47123e6de1bb6aa68e480cf54aafd756085ad52355ede.png)" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $\\angle CAD.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overrightarrow{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(\\angle BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $\\angle CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(\\angle BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(\\angle BAC).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx = 90^\\circ - 35^\\circ = 55^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110381 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "782a6a0a-7a15-5230-8f9d-5405aa72f96a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Combined Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "361d828c-ec57-5baa-81c6-321e0dc723e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-2577" :question/problem "In the figure below, determine $m\\angle{POR}.$\n\n![](images/0b/0bb38727216cc66882b7ed55fa59c3c700243ad18eb035a3e19a73eeffa81a2a.png)" :question/worked-solution "![](images/70/70bb672243a7689bd08c2d03ebe19570fdb148182dd7b5137da5be4b91724f03.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $\\angle{POQ}$ and $\\angle{QOR}$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overrightarrow{OQ}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠POR & =m∠POQ+m∠QOR \\\\  & ={68}^{∘}+{37}^{∘} \\\\  & ={105}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110382 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c59421f9-a1af-59d9-aa89-16cd2d13d332" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of an Unknown Angle Using the Extended Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "4ad9432d-82fc-58e6-b586-f16474fa18f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-2578" :question/problem "In the figure below, $m \\angle BAE = {110}^{\\circ}.$ Find the value of $x.$\n\n![](images/24/245dbaa430eb99aee193110fcd6df2844cfd7cffd2363c561337ac74d18a1fb5.png)" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $\\angle CAD.$\n\nThe measure of $\\angle CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(\\angle BAE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(\\angle BAC$ and $\\angle DAE).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx = 110^\\circ - 40^\\circ - 20^\\circ = 50^\\circ.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e8c4c24-2d04-5fd1-a9f4-6f1abb25c255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Smaller Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d60d52-b89a-5800-9afe-9fabc3d3d7ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={40}^{∘}\\times {90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432390} {:answer/id #uuid "788fca5f-3480-5c30-904f-476d2524db5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={90}^{∘}-{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432409} {:answer/id #uuid "7e6eee7f-4f55-5d36-99c4-c4fac6a6848d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={40}^{∘}+{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432411} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ba9fe0-5123-57e3-9161-7d6d17d14360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={90}^{∘}+{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432435} {:answer/id #uuid "f62bc2b1-11d0-535f-9873-c40886ddd516" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={40}^{∘}-{90}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432439}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "788fca5f-3480-5c30-904f-476d2524db5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={90}^{∘}-{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432409} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef70b5dc-8003-5cad-8bc8-e75e2766fb95" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8df2efb5-d399-5afd-8217-2b502698df60" :question/math-academy-id "q-150699" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b884ae8109d723e9277daa7b076d8a4ff52c07c8295e83d360a07bbb7785dd1d.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $m∠BAD={90}^{∘}.$ What equation could be used to find the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠BAC.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠BAC$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠CAD).$\n\nTherefore, the correct equation to determine $x$ is the following:\n\n$$\nx={90}^{∘}-{40}^{∘}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432457 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "782a6a0a-7a15-5230-8f9d-5405aa72f96a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Combined Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d7c93e-855d-5840-b285-e8b2de86a4d0" :an