S+m∠SOT \\\\  & ={55}^{∘}+{66}^{∘} \\\\  & ={121}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e8c4c24-2d04-5fd1-a9f4-6f1abb25c255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Smaller Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cf5e805-a9d8-501f-9421-02c871c68332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={30}^{∘}-{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432392} {:answer/id #uuid "8026e352-ae01-5b9e-908e-f8cba6fafc4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={70}^{∘}\\times {30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432413} {:answer/id #uuid "8bf7872a-2c29-5faa-80ca-39621ac3247c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={70}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432415} {:answer/id #uuid "9375889e-3849-59d0-ae4d-d04ee45ddd27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={70}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432417} {:answer/id #uuid "b25b3182-99f3-5733-be98-3b75b07c3ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={30}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9375889e-3849-59d0-ae4d-d04ee45ddd27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={70}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432417} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fbfac83-f221-5199-afc1-0a4537739b09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "22b396b3-caeb-5440-bb61-ec5206652aa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-150765" :question/problem "![](images/d8/d8552636c6f68b4885bf8a30bb8611629c0891ddc8c61cd27ff43c95cf6057bd.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $m∠BAD={70}^{∘}.$ What equation could be used to find the value of $x?$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠BAC.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠BAC$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠CAD).$\n\nTherefore, the correct equation to determine $x$ is the following:\n\n$$\nx={70}^{∘}-{30}^{∘}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432459 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e8c4c24-2d04-5fd1-a9f4-6f1abb25c255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Smaller Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "639e261a-02d5-509d-8b25-6646fedeecf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432404} {:answer/id #uuid "7138682c-63ce-54a0-b466-df6d68bf0255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432408} {:answer/id #uuid "8e013960-5f20-5489-8ad0-1fda062c79f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432416} {:answer/id #uuid "af12c256-412b-55f2-ab62-1d721dbffd84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{170}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432424} {:answer/id #uuid "f0073151-722a-59a3-b73c-920d6bd1dd42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7138682c-63ce-54a0-b466-df6d68bf0255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432408} :answer-field/id #uuid "72353706-d84b-5582-8ba8-ead7370acdc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c5fb27fa-76aa-58be-a097-af719acb9917" :question/math-academy-id "q-150767" :question/problem "![](images/de/de5601836d150d370b9ab7b8d0dceb76bcd0174f77f930f01fb488b772fcbcc6.png)\n\nThe measure of the angle $∠BAD$ is ${100}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠CAD.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAC$ and $∠CAD$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AC}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAD)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAC$ and $∠CAD).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠CAD$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAD)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAC).$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx={100}^{∘}-{70}^{∘}={30}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432463 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110671 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e8c4c24-2d04-5fd1-a9f4-6f1abb25c255" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Smaller Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522cb4ec-eb5a-56f1-a309-7a056515cc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{70}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432401} {:answer/id #uuid "62340687-3fc2-5a2f-944a-909d5d677a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{60}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432403} {:answer/id #uuid "7c