6432441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "461025dd-2d02-5f63-a292-225c3460091c" :question/math-academy-id "q-154877" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e3fe548e2dd695d682dec13287307e58fe28aa8a01b3e672695ef8ed07c61e1d.png)\n\nThe measure of the angle $∠BAE$ is ${150}^{∘}.$ Find the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the letter $x$ represents the measure of the unknown angle $∠DAE.$\n\nNote the following:\n\n- The angles $∠BAD$ and $∠DAE$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{AD}.$\n\n- So, the measure of the *large* angle $(∠BAE)$ must be the *sum* of the measures of the two *smaller* angles $(∠BAD$ and $∠DAE).$\n\n- This means that the measure of $∠DAE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAE)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx={150}^{∘}-{110}^{∘}={40}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110750 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c59421f9-a1af-59d9-aa89-16cd2d13d332" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of an Unknown Angle Using the Extended Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f249e0c-668b-5be1-b8ff-16f87f4d5391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f249e0c-668b-5be1-b8ff-16f87f4d5391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432393} :answer-field/id #uuid "15bea92c-fa20-58d1-9617-d5a73063267b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e0ae28b7-07ff-5372-8c05-3a6fb2ad772e" :question/math-academy-id "q-171825" :question/problem "![](images/89/89a4eb747c82276f349350f48ac2b711e1a308702eb1c717fbeacf79dbdad84f.png)\n\nIn the figure above, $m∠BAE={185}^{∘},$ $m∠BAD={120}^{∘},$ $m∠CAD={70}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$m∠CAE=$\n{{field-1}} ${}^{∘}.$" :question/worked-solution "The measure of $∠DAE$ must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠BAE)$ and the smaller known angle $(∠BAD).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nm∠DAE={185}^{∘}-{120}^{∘}={65}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add this to our diagram:\n\n![](images/fb/fb782eecfe7280c5808c8f0a42dbe0daec4110d94aa373271a03311dd0a0ead0.png)\n\nWe can now find the measure of $∠CAE:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠CAE & =m∠CAD+m∠DAE \\\\  & ={70}^{∘}+{65}^{∘} \\\\  & ={135}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110954 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "782a6a0a-7a15-5230-8f9d-5405aa72f96a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Combined Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "150dcf2e-cf5d-580c-80cf-4de132de6ddb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{114}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432378} {:answer/id #uuid "5c635d44-f527-52b7-8ae0-be4f7a219e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432402} {:answer/id #uuid "820cb5ee-19b1-5f2b-9761-e32669a23448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{110}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432414} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cea861-4883-5b3d-9ff5-0bc5b21f4817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{102}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432434} {:answer/id #uuid "ffd5e54d-ea4c-5c63-8f8e-9e59e4fa7ca4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{105}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820cb5ee-19b1-5