must be the *difference* between the large angle $(∠AFE)$ and the two smaller known angles $(∠CFD$ and $∠AFC).$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nx={144}^{∘}-{82}^{∘}-{25}^{∘}={37}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432455 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "782a6a0a-7a15-5230-8f9d-5405aa72f96a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Combined Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "126909ba-3771-5f25-a383-19d63b8ff86c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{104}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432376} {:answer/id #uuid "1ecc7cb4-cbf2-5870-9c08-126e39b3e1c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{100}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432382} {:answer/id #uuid "3282a89a-d584-573f-9da0-e3bcf36d0e87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{94}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432389} {:answer/id #uuid "3f585cc1-a3a3-5c4f-acfe-257243a61079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{98}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432394} {:answer/id #uuid "a16e2c60-5092-577d-82c4-b9a31f6d3fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{114}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "126909ba-3771-5f25-a383-19d63b8ff86c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{104}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432376} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5644df-5214-51b3-b065-807ab881aa7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39939039-dfca-5f99-86f6-773331c4950d" :question/math-academy-id "q-53142" :question/problem "![](images/7e/7e365bb8c51729748b0efdb54f50459859a382cba1def4b32b4009b3bde89dbd.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find $m∠COE.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/ae/ae007a68607a96bfd78986eeae11e69a4c8bd8dba35e8997933885d2ff1dc29f.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $∠COD$ and $∠DOE$ are adjacent because they share the side $\\overset{\\to }{OD}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠COE & =m∠COD+m∠DOE \\\\  & ={45}^{∘}+{59}^{∘} \\\\  & ={104}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432461 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110748 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "782a6a0a-7a15-5230-8f9d-5405aa72f96a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Measure of a Combined Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29cfb2bf-06d4-573d-9bee-ffd5e788ec1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{173}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432385} {:answer/id #uuid "30be3a32-c98a-5a2e-815d-43e60c1cf69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{170}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432387} {:answer/id #uuid "bdc851a8-8b03-5533-ad12-1db837de099d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{178}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432429} {:answer/id #uuid "c216af39-1fdd-5b20-80cf-2890b0736f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{152}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432431} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbf5eef-3692-5bca-8590-d7a98dc8ca44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{165}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30be3a32-c98a-5a2e-815d-43e60c1cf69b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{170}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432387} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f56c442-d0b3-53bb-a200-6ca894f18ad6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8c7b1f1-384a-5a9f-b6ee-9ff5d00c5514" :question/math-academy-id "q-53144" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cdd582f661cc05dd7e11cd6e104ccccb75e0b008b1144c1d1e6a97c7b07b7a1e.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of  $\\overset{^}{BOD}?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/e1/e1b8785260860f4946a7d0ca93a78fa2bddb5cbea95bcd841c75b3f53b5f1890.png)\n\nFirst, notice that $\\overset{^}{BOC}$ and $\\overset{^}{COD}$ are adjacent because they share the same side $\\overset{\\to }{OC}.$\n\nWe can add the measures of two adjacent angles to find the measure of the combined angle.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m\\overset{^}{BOD} & =m\\overset{^}{BOC}+m\\overset{^}{COD} \\\\  & ={100}^{∘}+{70}^{∘} \\\\  & ={170}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
